            "display_label_zh": "Scalar reward of the selected action",
            "domain_ref": "ONX_KERNEL_MATERN_INF_UNKNOWN_dom_285f934f79",
            "feedback_quality": {
              "feedback": "one scalar y_t=f_t(x_t)+z_t",
              "noise": "z_t iid N(0,sigma^2), independent of algorithm",
              "queries": "only played point"
            },
            "id": "ONX_KERNEL_MATERN_INF_UNKNOWN_ora_b85b5ff97b",
            "operation_code": "selected_reward",
            "query_signature": "Choose $x_t\\in[0,1]^d$ and then observe one noisy value at that point: $$Y_t=f_t(x_t)+Z_t,\\qquad Z_t\\overset{\\mathrm{i.i.d.}}\\sim\\mathcal N(0,\\sigma^2).$$. Noise is independent across rounds and independent of the algorithm; only the current action point is observed. Causal randomized policies are allowed and $d,T,k,B,\\sigma$ is public. The drift budget is hidden, so the same policy cannot depend on $V_\\infty$. Received feedback may be stored and reused computationally. No unrevealed historical information or extra queries to exhausted samples are available; any within-round full-function or common-sample access must be explicit.",
